      "section_id": "S1_HOOK",
      "voiceover_text": "Across the world, conversations about artificial intelligence are raising a central question: what does it mean for technology to serve people? to the internet, leading to further divide exclusion in AI usage. Those already connected are faced with the challenge of meaningful connectivity, which means to allow users to have a safe sex-fying and productive online experience, which to be enabled by digital literacy skills and competences. An example is our project on inclusive hiring and digital skills development, which counted systemic unemployment and exclusion by demonstrating how AI can make hiring practices fairer and digital skills more accessible. Another example is the inaugural AI and data science boot camp, where we built AI literacy amongst underrepresented groups to help redress intersectional gender imbalances and broaden participation in digital economies."
