      "section_id": "S2_CONTEXT",
      "voiceover_text": "But the arrival of AI in Access Age does not resolve the underlying tensions. It often sharpens them — exposing who has voice, who has access, and who bears the risks. Thank you, modelators, Amber Funner and the O attendees, ladies and gentlemen. I am Esther Simon-Negamba, who I'm working at the Recology of Business Education in the restaurant city in Tanzania, in Africa. Without this crucial step of actually implementing datasets that showcase a wide variety of individuals, communities, and cultures and challenging personally held biases, the possibility of using this technology with an inclusion work becomes more complex. As the implications of using something that could cause harm need to be considered and handled. of us with these new digital technologies, I now respect the youth. Let's today's discussion, self-execord to action, for policy makers to embrace inclusive governance of AI, for academia and innovators to prioritize ethical and climate conscious applications, for the civil society to keep raising awareness on how technology intersects with rights and access."
