      "section_id": "S3_EVIDENCE",
      "voiceover_text": "Across these conversations, Access Age is not a distant aspiration. It is a field in motion — with real evidence, real failure, and real possibilities for change. continued contribution to the International Day for Universal Access to Information that we are celebrating in the 28th of September. This year, the main theme is ensuring access to environmental information in the digital age as you know, essential topic for the planet. Equally important is the inclusion of women, rural communities and persons with disabilities. These groups must not remain on the margins of digital development. Hello everyone, I'm very happy to join you today for this conference on artificial intelligence for information accessibility. And I want to take the opportunity of this short talk to specifically address the dimensions of gender inclusion in the AI economy which I think is really relevant and connected to the topics discussed in this conference."
