      "voiceover_text": "The measure of AI will not be the speed of its systems, but whether the people it touches are better served, better heard, and more free. is also about enlightened access. So let us all put our shoulders to the wheel and start to address critical needs such as digital media and information literacy. And we believe that AI is undoubtedly a technology of our time, but as the title of this panel suggests we cannot find blind, and its costs are not fully clear and neither are its benefits. It is therefore essential to ensure that benefits are fairly distributed, and that costs do not fall in the most vulnerable populations."
